  "explanation": [
    "$10^4 = 10 \\times 10 \\times 10 \\times 10 = 10{,}000$.",
    "Multiplying by $10{,}000$ adds four zeros to the end of $62$.",
    "$62 \\to 620 \\to 6{,}200 \\to 62{,}000 \\to 620{,}000$, so the answer is $620{,}000$ (C)."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Why the other choices are off",
      "steps": [
        "$6{,}200$ came from only two shifts, and $62{,}000$ from three.",
        "$6{,}200{,}000$ came from five.",
        "The exponent $4$ tells you exactly four shifts."
